  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready, with six questions on O4. The quiz is in `quizzes/0002.json` and its key is in `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **What it covers:** who owns the control flow in a workflow and in an agent, and when a fixed workflow is the better choice. The examples come from the makerspace assistant: booking steps, cost per request and a failing 3D print.\n- **Format:** five multiple-choice items and one short-answer item. One of the multiple-choice items asks you to work out a cost difference in model calls. The difficulty rises through the quiz, and the last item asks you to judge which task suits an agent.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** there is no lesson on O4 yet, so this quiz checks the objective itself. It draws on the workflow-versus-agent distinction in Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\", which I wrote from memory and did not re-read or search for this session.\n- **Misconception ids:** the key has no `distractors` entries. The workspace has no definitions for the misconception ids used in quiz 0001, so I didn't guess at ids for these wrong options.\n\nQuiz 0001 is still ungraded, with two submissions waiting. Do you want me to grade those next, or give you a lesson on O4 before you take this quiz?",
